  "term": "AComA",
  "definition": "AComA stands for the anterior communicating artery complex, a brain blood vessel region described here as one of the most common sites where intracranial aneurysms occur. In this assessment context, it is discussed in relation to estimating aneurysm rupture risk by considering blood flow and vessel wall mechanics.",
